window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"vladimir","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-5","text":"The whole lane is a cooldown chess match: Transfusion heals his nail chip, and Ashen Pursuit is his only mobility on a 10s timer - the ten seconds after he spends it is the window you fight in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Purgatory is 120s at rank 1 and executes below a threshold - stay above the floor, or spend Pool's 2 untargetable seconds inside the zone."},{"when":"1st item","text":"It stays close, but your sustain starts clawing the lane back - each Transfusion undoes his poke faster than he can reapply it."},{"when":"Late","text":"You outscale outright: Hemoplague amp plus drain-tank healing wins every extended fight his burst cannot end instantly."}],"wants":{"you":["Pool saved for his blink-in and the execute","Transfusion weaves that undo his nail chip","The long game where drain outscales burst"],"foe":["Baiting Pool, then Ashen Pursuit onto a marked you","R Purgatory placed while your Pool is down","Ending the game before Hemoplague takes over"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are an honest skill lane: his burst threat and your escape tools cancel out, so it becomes a dance of cooldowns - weave Transfusion on his nail whiffs, never Pool for harassment you can heal back, and drop your mark stacks before three, because his attacks cash them in for bonus damage.","mid":"Nothing separates you through 4-6 unless someone blinks: he wants marks on you, then Ashen Pursuit in for the bite, with Purgatory to execute what is left. Hold Sanguine Pool's 2 seconds for exactly that arrival, heal everything else, and Soul Ignition's self-damage window is where Grievous Wounds pays.","late":"First item stays close but the current has turned - your sustain claws back every trade, and from two items on you simply outscale him: Hemoplague's amp turns fights into team-wide executions, Pool laughs at his totem timing, and drain-tank healing grinds through burst that no longer one-rotations you.","whys":["An even skill lane at 1 - his burst threat and your escape tools cancel out.","Trades stay balanced around your Pool and Transfusion cooldowns at 2.","Level 3 remains a skill fight over whether he can bait out your escapes.","Neither side pulls clearly ahead through levels 4-5.","At 6 your untargetable Pool trades evenly against his execute totem.","First item stays close, but your sustain begins clawing the lane back.","Late, your drains and Hemoplague amp outscale his burst completely."]});
