window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"vladimir","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-5","text":"A long even stretch: your Transfusion sustain and E zoning offset his Q The Darkin Glaive poke, and neither of you can force a kill without the other misplaying."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hemoplague amp versus his R Grim Deliverance is pure execution - it heals him off the damage, so land anti-heal before your ult swings the fight."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first AP item is the takeover point: Q and E become real burst, and Sanguine Pool now dodges the all-in he needs to land to stay relevant."},{"when":"2 items","text":"You are a full drain-tank - Pool plus spell-vamp healing means his bruiser DPS can no longer race your sustain, so take every extended fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Safe scaling into your first AP item","Pool timed onto his R Grim Deliverance","Extended fights where drain beats bruiser DPS"],"foe":["Kill pressure before your item spike lands","E Aureate Rush burst while Pool is down","A short game that ends before you outscale"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are an even poke lane - nothing committal is online for either of you, so trade Q for Q and keep the wave in a safe spot. Level 3 through 5 stays a skill check: his glaive poke stings against your low base HP, but Transfusion undoes it and your E charge zones him off free engages.","mid":"Level 6 changes the stakes but not the balance: Hemoplague turns any extended fight your way, while his R Grim Deliverance heals him back through a mistimed Pool - whoever lands their ultimate on their own terms wins the all-in, so play it patient and make him move first.","late":"Your first AP item is where the lane tips for good - Q and E become genuine burst and Pool invalidates the all-in window he spent all lane building toward. By two items you are a scaling drain-tank he cannot solve: his Q and R healing lose the race once Grievous Wounds is on him, and Hemoplague ends his teamfights.","whys":["Level 1 is an even poke lane with no committal tools online for either side.","Level 2 stays neutral - you trade pokes but neither of you can commit.","Level 3 is a skill fight: your Q poke and Transfusion sustain offset his glaive, and your E zoning holds the line.","Levels 4-5 remain a skill check - your low base HP and his burst balance against your healing.","Level 6 stays even: your Hemoplague amp versus his R lockdown comes down to execution.","On your first AP item you spike ahead - Q and E become real burst and Pool dodges his all-in.","Two items in you are a scaling drain-tank whose Pool and lifesteal make you the stronger sustained duelist."]});
